": 23.76, "end": 24.4}, {"text": "Hij", "type": "word", "start": 24.72, "end": 24.8}, {"text": "wacht", "type": "word", "start": 24.88, "end": 25.12}, {"text": "bij", "type": "word", "start": 25.2, "end": 25.28}, {"text": "een", "type": "word", "start": 25.36, "end": 25.44}, {"text": "gat", "type": "word", "start": 25.48, "end": 25.68}, {"text": "in", "type": "word", "start": 25.72, "end": 25.76}, {"text": "het", "type": "word", "start": 25.84, "end": 25.92}, {"text": "ijs,", "type": "word", "start": 26, "end": 26.36}, {"text": "waar", "type": "word", "start": 26.4, "end": 26.48}, {"text": "de", "type": "word", "start": 26.52, "end": 26.56}, {"text": "zeehond", "type": "word", "start": 26.64, "end": 27.04}, {"text": "komt", "type": "word", "start": 27.12, "end": 27.36}, {"text": "ademen.", "type": "word", "start": 27.44, "end": 27.84}, {"text": "Zeehonden,", "type": "word", "start": 28.4, "end": 29.2}, {"text": "vissen,", "type": "word", "start": 29.28, "end": 29.92}, {"text": "andere", "type": "word", "start": 30, "end": 30.24}, {"text": "ijsberen:", "type": "word", "start": 30.32, "end": 31.36}, {"text": "dat", "type": "word", "start": 31.44, "end": 31.52}, {"text": "zijn", "type": "word", "start": 31.56, "end": 31.84}, {"text": "levende", "type": "word", "start": 31.96, "end": 32.32}, {"text": "dingen", "type": "word", "start": 32.4, "end": 32.56}, {"text": "om", "type": "word", "start": 32.64, "end": 32.72}, {"text": "hem", "type": "word", "start": 32.8, "end": 32.88}, {"text": "heen.", "type": "word", "start": 32.92, "end": 33.2}, {"text": "We", "type": "word", "start": 33.52, "end": 33.6}, {"text": "noemen", "type": "word", "start": 33.68, "end": 33.84}, {"text": "ze", "type": "word", "start": 33.92, "end": 34.08}, {"text": "biotische", "type": "word", "start": 34.32, "end": 34.96}, {"text": "factoren.", "type": "word", "start": 35.04, "end": 35.92}], "text": "Het antwoord is cee. De woestijn is te heet voor hem. En er is niets te eten. Kijk naar waar een ijsbeer wel woont. Het is er koud, tot min veertig graden. Een groot deel van het jaar ligt er ijs op de zee. Kou, ijs, zout water, sneeuw: dat zijn dingen zonder leven. We noemen ze abiotische factoren. Een ijsbeer jaagt op zeehonden. Hij wacht bij een gat in het ijs, waar de zeehond komt ademen. Zeehonden, vissen, andere ijsberen: dat zijn levende dingen om hem heen. We noemen ze biotische factoren."}